      "writtenOn": "2026-10-21T15:35:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the suggestion. I think it would be good to keep `Configuration.\u003cType\u003e` as the key services discover their entries by, since watching for it lets the mapper filter by type rather than each service reading the `Type` of every entry, and it spares services from tracking endpoints themselves. \n`Name` and `Type` could then live only on `Configuration.Exposes`, and I\u0027d be happy to drop them from Configuration.\u003cType\u003e in a follow-up once consumers such as the dbus-sensors, pldm, spdm daemons read them from there. \nWould that work for you, or do you have something else in mind?",
      "parentUuid": "2eb5b4e8_775a8ca9",
      "revId": "441ada7b20ec5a2a0870c70c1354ff7803ec6031",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
